-- Clean up junk rows in notification_deliveries that made the Admin Portal
-- Notification Log unusable (see admin.hakkiu.com/monitoring/notifications).
--
-- Two sources of noise are removed here:
--
-- 1) TEST DATA — rows generated by hitting the case-status endpoint with a fake
--    case_id of 'test-case-123'. dispatch_notifications() correctly recorded them
--    as skipped ("could not resolve org from case test-case-123"), but they are
--    pure test residue polluting production history.
--
-- 2) PHANTOM "SENT" ROWS — routes/monitoring.py used to call log_delivery(ok=True)
--    a SECOND time after dispatch_notifications() (which already logs its own row).
--    That wrote a bogus "sent" row for EVERY escalate/dismiss even when the real
--    dispatch was skipped — with no recipient, subject or body. A genuine sent
--    case_escalated always has recipient + subject populated by _sent(), and a
--    case_dismissed is ALWAYS skipped (never legitimately "sent"), so these
--    predicates only match the duplicate bug rows. The code bug is fixed in the
--    same change; this removes the historical residue.

-- 1) Test residue (matches both the payload case_id and the skip-reason text).
DELETE FROM public.notification_deliveries
WHERE payload->>'case_id' = 'test-case-123'
   OR error_message LIKE '%test-case-123%';

-- 2) Phantom "sent" duplicates from the double-logging bug.
DELETE FROM public.notification_deliveries
WHERE status = 'sent'
  AND recipient IS NULL
  AND subject IS NULL
  AND event_type IN ('case_escalated', 'case_dismissed');
